{"id":"gph-fig-007","s":"physics","t":"4.4.2.3","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the activity of two sources, A and B, which start with the same activity. At 20 minutes, how many times bigger is the activity of B than the activity of A?","o":["0.5 times","4 times","2 times","200 times"],"a":2,"x":"At 20 minutes, read B: 400 Bq. Read A: 200 Bq. Divide B by A: 400 ÷ 200 = 2. B has the longer half-life, so its activity is 2 times bigger.","w":["Divides A by B, so the ratio is upside down. B is the larger activity.","Compares the curves at 40 minutes, not 20 minutes, where A has fallen further.","","Subtracts the activities (400 − 200) and gives the difference in Bq as if it were a ratio."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,40],"y":[0,800],"xstep":5,"ystep":100,"xlabel":"time / minutes","ylabel":"activity / Bq","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,800.0],[0.25,786.256479],[0.5,772.749063],[0.75,759.473697],[1.0,746.426393],[1.25,733.603235],[1.5,721.00037],[1.75,708.614015],[2.0,696.440451],[2.25,684.476021],[2.5,672.717132],[2.75,661.160255],[3.0,649.801917],[3.25,638.638709],[3.5,627.667278],[3.75,616.88433],[4.0,606.286627],[4.25,595.870985],[4.5,585.634278],[4.75,575.573432],[5.0,565.685425],[5.25,555.967288],[5.5,546.416103],[5.75,537.029001],[6.0,527.803164],[6.25,518.735822],[6.5,509.824251],[6.75,501.065775],[7.0,492.457765],[7.25,483.997636],[7.5,475.682846],[7.75,467.510899],[8.0,459.479342],[8.25,451.585762],[8.5,443.827789],[8.75,436.203093],[9.0,428.709385],[9.25,421.344414],[9.5,414.10597],[9.75,406.991877],[10.0,400.0],[10.25,393.128239],[10.5,386.374532],[10.75,379.736848],[11.0,373.213197],[11.25,366.801617],[11.5,360.500185],[11.75,354.307008],[12.0,348.220225],[12.25,342.23801],[12.5,336.358566],[12.75,330.580127],[13.0,324.900959],[13.25,319.319355],[13.5,313.833639],[13.75,308.442165],[14.0,303.143313],[14.25,297.935493],[14.5,292.817139],[14.75,287.786716],[15.0,282.842712],[15.25,277.983644],[15.5,273.208051],[15.75,268.514501],[16.0,263.901582],[16.25,259.367911],[16.5,2