{"id":"gph-fig-003","s":"physics","t":"4.5.6.1.5","lv":1,"q":"A car's journey is shown on the graph. What is the car's acceleration during the first part of the journey, while the line slopes upwards?","o":["0.5 m/s²","1.1 m/s²","2.0 m/s²","16 m/s²"],"a":2,"x":"Acceleration is the gradient of a velocity-time graph. The velocity rises from 0 to 16 m/s in 8 s. $a = \\frac{16}{8} = 2.0$ m/s².","w":["Divided time by velocity (8 ÷ 16). This turns the gradient upside down.","Used 14 s, the end of the flat part, as the time. The speeding-up part ends at 8 s.","","Read the top velocity off the graph and gave it as the acceleration, without dividing by time."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,16],"y":[0,20],"xstep":2,"ystep":4,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"velocity / m/s","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[8,16],[14,16],[16,0]],"c":0}],"points":[{"at":[8,16],"label":"P"}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gph-fig-004","s":"physics","t":"4.5.6.1.5","lv":2,"q":"A cyclist is already moving at the start of the graph. Use the graph to find the distance the cyclist travels while the velocity is rising.","o":["60 m","96 m","36 m","24 m"],"a":0,"x":"Distance is the area under the graph. The rising part is a trapezium: start velocity 4 m/s, end velocity 16 m/s, time 6 s. Area = ½ × (4 + 16) × 6 = 60 m.","w":["","Used the top velocity of 16 m/s for the whole 6 s. That treats the velocity as constant and gives too much.","Found only the triangle above the starting velocity (½ × 6 × 12). The rectangle under it was left out.","Used only the starting velocity of 4 m/s for 6 s. The rise in velocity was ignored."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,10],"y":[0,20],"xstep":2,"ystep":4,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"velocity / m/s","lines":[{"pts":[[0,4],[6,16],[10,16]],"c":0}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gph-fig-005","s":"physics","t":"4.5.6.1.5","lv":3,"q":"Cars A and B both travel for the full time shown on the graph. How much further does car B travel than car A?","o":["8 m","64 m","96 m","32 m"],"a":3,"x":"Distance is the area under each line. A: ½ × 8 × 16 = 64 m. B: ½ × (8 + 16) × 8 = 96 m. Difference = 96 − 64 = 32 m.","w":["Read the gap between the starting velocities. That is a velocity, not a distance.","Found A's distance only. The question asks for the difference between the two cars.","Found B's distance only. A's distance of 64 m must be subtracted.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,8],"y":[0,16],"xstep":1,"ystep":2,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"velocity / m/s","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[8,16]],"label":"A","c":0},{"pts":[[0,8],[8,16]],"label":"B","c":1}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gph-fig-008","s":"physics","t":"4.2.1","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the current against potential difference for a resistor at constant temperature. Use point P to work out the resistance of the resistor.","o":["0.067 Ω","2.4 Ω","15 Ω","5.6 Ω"],"a":2,"x":"At P the potential difference is 6 V and the current is 0.4 A. Resistance = potential difference ÷ current (R = V ÷ I) = 6 ÷ 0.4 = 15 Ω.","w":["Divided current by potential difference (0.4 ÷ 6), which is the equation upside down.","Multiplied potential difference by current (6 × 0.4) instead of dividing.","","Subtracted the current from the potential difference (6 − 0.4) instead of dividing."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,6],"y":[0,0.5],"xstep":1,"ystep":0.1,"xlabel":"potential difference / V","ylabel":"current / A","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[6,0.4]],"c":0}],"points":[{"at":[6,0.4],"label":"P"}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gph-fig-009","s":"physics","t":"4.2.1","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows the current–potential difference line for a diode. The diode is connected the wrong way round to a 1.5 V cell. Use the graph to find the current that flows.","o":["40 mA","10 mA","1.5 mA","0 mA"],"a":3,"x":"Connected the wrong way round, the p.d. across the diode is −1.5 V. On the graph the line is flat on the axis for negative p.d. So the current is 0 mA. A diode only lets current through one way.","w":["Read the forward side of the graph at +1.5 V, ignoring that the diode is reversed.","Read the current at 1.0 V instead of using the reversed p.d. of −1.5 V.","Used the 1.5 V as if it were a current in mA. The current axis must be read from the line.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[-2,2],"y":[-10,40],"xstep":0.5,"ystep":10,"xlabel":"potential difference / V","ylabel":"current / mA","lines":[{"pts":[[-2,0],[0,0],[0.5,0],[0.75,2],[1,10],[1.25,22],[1.5,40]],"c":0}],"points":[],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gph-fig-033","s":"physics","t":"4.5.6.1","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows a girl's walk from home to a shop and back home. She stops at the shop for a while. What is her average speed for the whole walk?","o":["0 m/s","0.8 m/s","1.6 m/s","2.0 m/s"],"a":2,"x":"Total distance = 400 m there + 400 m back = 800 m. Total time = 500 s, including the stop. Average speed = 800 ÷ 500 = 1.6 m/s.","w":["She is back at the start, so displacement is 0. This gives average velocity, not average speed.","Used only the 400 m to the shop, not the 800 m for the whole walk, then divided by 500 s.","","Found her speed on the way to the shop (400 ÷ 200) instead of the average for the whole walk."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,600],"y":[0,500],"xstep":100,"ystep":100,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"distance from home / m","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[200,400],[300,400],[500,0]],"c":0}],"points":[],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gph-fig-034","s":"physics","t":"4.5.6.1","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows a trolley speeding up. The dashed line is a tangent to the curve at P. What is the speed of the trolley at P?","o":["2.0 m/s","4.0 m/s","8.0 m/s","0.25 m/s"],"a":1,"x":"Speed at a point is the gradient of the tangent. The tangent passes through (2 s, 0 m) and (7 s, 20 m). Gradient = 20 ÷ 5 = 4.0 m/s.","w":["Divided the distance at P by the time at P (8 ÷ 4). That gives average speed from the start, not speed at P.","","Read the distance at P off the axis and gave it as a speed.","Turned the gradient upside down (time ÷ distance), so 5 ÷ 20 gives 0.25."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,8],"y":[0,32],"xstep":1,"ystep":4,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"distance / m","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[0.05,0.00125],[0.1,0.005],[0.15,0.01125],[0.2,0.02],[0.25,0.03125],[0.3,0.045],[0.35,0.06125],[0.4,0.08],[0.45,0.10125],[0.5,0.125],[0.55,0.15125],[0.6,0.18],[0.65,0.21125],[0.7,0.245],[0.75,0.28125],[0.8,0.32],[0.85,0.36125],[0.9,0.405],[0.95,0.45125],[1.0,0.5],[1.05,0.55125],[1.1,0.605],[1.15,0.66125],[1.2,0.72],[1.25,0.78125],[1.3,0.845],[1.35,0.91125],[1.4,0.98],[1.45,1.05125],[1.5,1.125],[1.55,1.20125],[1.6,1.28],[1.65,1.36125],[1.7,1.445],[1.75,1.53125],[1.8,1.62],[1.85,1.71125],[1.9,1.805],[1.95,1.90125],[2.0,2.0],[2.05,2.10125],[2.1,2.205],[2.15,2.31125],[2.2,2.42],[2.25,2.53125],[2.3,2.645],[2.35,2.76125],[2.4,2.88],[2.45,3.00125],[2.5,3.125],[2.55,3.25125],[2.6,3.38],[2.65,3.51125],[2.7,3.645],[2.75,3.78125],[2.8,3.92],[2.85,4.06125],[2.9,4.205],[2.95,4.35125],[3.0,4.5],[3.05,4.65125],[3.1,4.805],[3.15,4.96125],[3.2,5.12],[3.25,5.28125],[3.3,5.445],[3.35,5.61125],[3.4,5.78],[3.45,5.95125],[3.5,6.125],[3.55,6.30125],[3.6,6.48],[3.65,6.66125],[3.7,6.845],[3.75,7.03125],[3.8,7.22],[3.85,7.41125],[3.9,7.605],[3.95,7.80125],[4.0,8.0],[4.05,8.20125],[4.1,8.405],[4.15,8.61125],[4.2,8.82],[4.25,9.03125],[4.3,9.245],[4.35,9.46125],[4.4,9.68],[4.45,9.90125],[4.5,10.125],[4.55,10.35125],[4.6,10.58],[4.65,10.811