{"id":"gph-fig-044","s":"physics","t":"4.6.1","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows a transverse wave on a rope at one moment. The wave has a frequency of 50 Hz. Use the graph to work out the wave speed.","o":["200 m/s","150 m/s","2.0 m/s","1.0 m/s"],"a":2,"x":"P and Q are neighbouring crests, so one wavelength is 8 − 4 = 4 cm = 0.04 m. Wave speed = frequency × wavelength = 50 × 0.04 = 2.0 m/s.","w":["Used 4 cm as the wavelength but did not change it to metres, so the answer is 100 times too big.","Used the amplitude, 3 cm, as the wavelength, then did not change cm to m.","","Used the crest to trough distance, 2 cm, which is only half a wavelength. 50 × 0.02 = 1.0 m/s."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,12],"y":[-4,4],"xstep":2,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"distance along rope / cm","ylabel":"displacement / cm","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,3.0],[0.075,2.979205],[0.15,2.91711],[0.225,2.814574],[0.3,2.67302],[0.375,2.494409],[0.45,2.281218],[0.525,2.036402],[0.6,1.763356],[0.675,1.465864],[0.75,1.14805],[0.825,0.814321],[0.9,0.469303],[0.975,0.117779],[1.05,-0.235377],[1.125,-0.585271],[1.2,-0.927051],[1.275,-1.255979],[1.35,-1.567496],[1.425,-1.857282],[1.5,-2.12132],[1.575,-2.355951],[1.65,-2.55792],[1.725,-2.72443],[1.8,-2.85317],[1.875,-2.942356],[1.95,-2.990752],[2.025,-2.997687],[2.1,-2.963065],[2.175,-2.887366],[2.25,-2.771639],[2.325,-2.617488],[2.4,-2.427051],[2.475,-2.202968],[2.55,-1.948344],[2.625,-1.666711],[2.7,-1.361971],[2.775,-1.038351],[2.85,-0.700336],[2.925,-0.352612],[3.0,-0.0],[3.075,0.352612],[3.15,0.700336],[3.225,1.038351],[3.3,1.361971],[3.375,1.666711],[3.45,1.948344],[3.525,2.202968],[3.6,2.427051],[3.675,2.617488],[3.75,2.771639],[3.825,2.887366],[3.9,2.963065],[3.975,2.997687],[4.05,2.990752],[4.125,2.942356],[4.2,2.85317],[4.275,2.72443],[4.35,2.55792],[4.425,2.355951],[4.5,2.12132],[4.575,1.857282],[4.65,1.567496],[4.725,1.255979],[4.8,0.927051],[4.875,0.585271],[4.95,0.235377],[5.025,-0.117779],[5.1,-0.469303],[5.175,-0.814321],[5.25,-1.14805],[5.325,-1.465864],[5.4