{"id":"gph-fig-045","s":"physics","t":"4.6.1","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows how the displacement of one point on a wave changes with time. Use the graph to find the frequency of the wave.","o":["125 Hz","0.125 Hz","500 Hz","8000 Hz"],"a":0,"x":"A and B are neighbouring crests, so the period is 10 − 2 = 8 ms = 0.008 s. Frequency = 1 ÷ period = 1 ÷ 0.008 = 125 Hz.","w":["","Used 8 as the period in seconds, so 1 ÷ 8 = 0.125 Hz. The time axis is in milliseconds.","Used the time to the first crest, 2 ms, as the period. 1 ÷ 0.002 = 500 Hz.","Multiplied the period in ms by 1000 instead of finding 1 ÷ period in seconds."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,16],"y":[-3,3],"xstep":2,"ystep":1,"xlabel":"time / ms","ylabel":"displacement / mm","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[0.1,0.156918],[0.2,0.312869],[0.3,0.466891],[0.4,0.618034],[0.5,0.765367],[0.6,0.907981],[0.7,1.044997],[0.8,1.175571],[0.9,1.298896],[1.0,1.414214],[1.1,1.520812],[1.2,1.618034],[1.3,1.70528],[1.4,1.782013],[1.5,1.847759],[1.6,1.902113],[1.7,1.94474],[1.8,1.975377],[1.9,1.993835],[2.0,2.0],[2.1,1.993835],[2.2,1.975377],[2.3,1.94474],[2.4,1.902113],[2.5,1.847759],[2.6,1.782013],[2.7,1.70528],[2.8,1.618034],[2.9,1.520812],[3.0,1.414214],[3.1,1.298896],[3.2,1.175571],[3.3,1.044997],[3.4,0.907981],[3.5,0.765367],[3.6,0.618034],[3.7,0.466891],[3.8,0.312869],[3.9,0.156918],[4.0,0.0],[4.1,-0.156918],[4.2,-0.312869],[4.3,-0.466891],[4.4,-0.618034],[4.5,-0.765367],[4.6,-0.907981],[4.7,-1.044997],[4.8,-1.175571],[4.9,-1.298896],[5.0,-1.414214],[5.1,-1.520812],[5.2,-1.618034],[5.3,-1.70528],[5.4,-1.782013],[5.5,-1.847759],[5.6,-1.902113],[5.7,-1.94474],[5.8,-1.975377],[5.9,-1.993835],[6.0,-2.0],[6.1,-1.993835],[6.2,-1.975377],[6.3,-1.94474],[6.4,-1.902113],[6.5,-1.847759],[6.6,-1.782013],[6.7,-1.70528],[6.8,-1.618034],[6.9,-1.520812],[7.0,-1.414214],[7.1,-1.298896],[7.2,-1.175571],[7.3,-1.044997],[7.4,-0.907981],[7.5,-0.765367],[7.6,-0.618034],[7.7,-0.466891],[7.8,-0.312869],[7.9,-0.156918],[8.0,-0.0],[8.1,0.156918],[8.2,0.31286