{"id":"gph-fig-046","s":"physics","t":"4.6.1","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows how far one wave crest travels along a stretched spring as time passes. The wave has a frequency of 1.5 Hz. Use the graph to find the wavelength.","o":["3.0 m","4.5 m","0.50 m","2.0 m"],"a":3,"x":"The gradient is the wave speed. At P: 18 m ÷ 6 s = 3.0 m/s. Wavelength = wave speed ÷ frequency = 3.0 ÷ 1.5 = 2.0 m.","w":["Gave the wave speed, the gradient, as the wavelength and did not use the frequency.","Multiplied speed by frequency, 3.0 × 1.5, instead of dividing speed by frequency.","Divided frequency by speed, 1.5 ÷ 3.0, which is the wrong way round.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,8],"y":[0,24],"xstep":1,"ystep":6,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"distance travelled / m","lines":[{"pts":[[0,0],[8,24]],"c":0}],"points":[{"at":[6,18],"label":"P"}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gph-fig-041","s":"physics","t":"4.5.6.3","lv":2,"q":"The bar chart shows one driver's reaction time in four conditions. The car travels at 15 m/s. How much further does it go before braking when the driver is on the phone than when alert?","o":["15 m","9 m","6 m","0.6 m"],"a":1,"x":"Read the bars: on phone 1.0 s, alert 0.4 s. The difference is 0.6 s. Extra thinking distance = speed × time = 15 × 0.6 = 9 m.","w":["Uses only the phone bar (1.0 s × 15 m/s) and does not subtract the alert driver's distance.","","Uses only the alert bar (0.4 s × 15 m/s) instead of the difference between the two bars.","Finds the difference in time (0.6 s) but does not multiply by speed, so the unit is wrong too."],"fig":{"type":"bar","cats":["Alert","Tired","On phone","Alcohol"],"vals":[0.4,0.8,1.0,1.4],"y":[0,1.6],"ystep":0.2,"xlabel":"driver condition","ylabel":"reaction time / s"}}
{"id":"gph-fig-042","s":"physics","t":"4.5.6.3","lv":2,"q":"The graph shows a car's speed from the moment the driver sees a hazard until the car stops. Use the graph to find the distance the car travels while the brakes are being applied.","o":["60 m","80 m","40 m","20 m"],"a":2,"x":"The brakes are on from 1 s to 5 s, as speed falls from 20 m/s to 0. Braking distance = area of the triangle = ½ × 4 s × 20 m/s = 40 m.","w":["Adds the thinking distance (20 m) as well, which gives the total stopping distance, not the braking distance.","Uses the full rectangle 4 s × 20 m/s and forgets the ½ for a triangle.","","Reads the flat part of the graph, which is the thinking distance (1 s × 20 m/s), not the braking distance."],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,6],"y":[0,24],"xstep":1,"ystep":4,"xlabel":"time / s","ylabel":"speed / m/s","lines":[{"pts":[[0,20],[1,20],[5,0]],"c":0}],"xnums":true,"ynums":true}}
{"id":"gph-fig-043","s":"physics","t":"4.5.6.3","lv":3,"q":"The graph shows braking distance against speed for the same car on a dry road and on a wet road. Compare the braking force on the wet road with the dry road at the same speed.","o":["Wet force is double the dry force","Wet force is the same as the dry force","Wet force is a quarter of the dry force","Wet force is half the dry force"],"a":3,"x":"At 20 m/s the dry distance is 20 m and the wet distance is 40 m. Same kinetic energy, and work done = force × distance. Twice the distance means half the force.","w":["Turns the ratio upside down. A longer braking distance means a smaller force, not a larger one.","Thinks the force is the same because the car and its speed are the same. The graph shows the stopping distances differ.","Squares the ratio. The distance is only 2 times longer (40 m against 20 m), so the force is half, not a quarter.",""],"fig":{"type":"graph","x":[0,30],"y":[0,90],"xstep":5,"ystep":10,"xlabel":"speed / m/s","ylabel":"braking distance / m","lines":[{"pts":[[0.0,0.0],[0.1875,0.001758],[0.375,0.007031],[0.5625,0.01582],[0.75,0.028125],[0.9375,0.043945],[1.125,0.063281],[1.3125,0.086133],[1.5,0.1125],[1.6875,0.142383],[1.875,0.175781],[2.0625,0.212695],[2.25,0.253125],[2.4375,0.29707],[2.625,0.344531],[2.8125,0.395508],[3.0,0.45],[3.1875,0.508008],[3.375,0.569531],[3.5625,0.63457],[3.75,0.703125],[3.9375,0.775195],[4.125,0.850781],[4.3125,0.929883],[4.5,1.0125],[4.6875,1.098633],[4.875,1.188281],[5.0625,1.281445],[5.25,1.378125],[5.4375,1.47832],[5.625,1.582031],[5.8125,1.689258],[6.0,1.8],[6.1875,1.914258],[6.375,2.032031],[6.5625,2.15332],[6.75,2.278125],[6.9375,2.406445],[7.125,2.538281],[7.3125,2.673633],[7.5,2.8125],[7.6875,2.954883],[7.875,3.100781],[8.0625,3.250195],[8.25,3.403125],[8.4375,3.55957],[8.625,3.719531],[8.8125,3.883008],[9.0,4.05],[9.1875,4.220508],[9.375,4.394531],[9.5625,4.57207],[9.75,4.753125],[9.9375,4.937695],[10.125,5.125781],[10.3125,5.317383],[10.5,5.5125],[10.68